tid="ppcart-admin-notice-integration-settings">settings page</a> to check your integration settings.</p>'=>'无法连接到以下列出的集成。请访问 %1$s <a href="%2$s" rel="noreferrer noopener" data-testid="ppcart-admin-notice-integration-settings">设置页面</a> 检查您的集成设置。','Stripe Connect is enabled, but the destination account is missing for the active API mode.'=>'Stripe Connect 已启用，但活动 API 模式缺少目标账户。','Use the Connect with Stripe button in Stripe settings to connect an account for this mode.'=>'在 Stripe 设置中使用“与 Stripe 连接”按钮来连接此模式的账户。','Stripe Connect destination account format is invalid.'=>'Stripe Connect 目标账户格式无效。','Use a connected account ID that starts with acct_. Values like ca_ are not valid destinations.'=>'使用以 acct_ 开头的连接账户 ID。像 ca_ 这样的值不是有效的目标。','Stripe reconnect required for the active API mode.'=>'活动 API 模式需要重新连接 Stripe。','Stripe keys are missing or not readable. Use Connect with Stripe to sync direct keys.'=>'缺少或无法读取 Stripe 密钥。使用“与 Stripe 连接”来同步直接密钥。','Stripe is using legacy credentials that are not stored as direct Stripe keys. Use Connect with Stripe before removing payment decryptor support.'=>'Stripe 正在使用未作为直接 Stripe 密钥存储的旧凭据。在移除支付解密器支持之前，请使用 Stripe 连接。','Stripe secret key is missing for the active API mode.'=>'活动 API 模式缺少 Stripe 秘密密钥。','Connect status could not be verified without a Stripe secret key.'=>'没有 Stripe 秘密密钥，无法验证连接状态。','Stripe Connect status:'=>'Stripe 连接状态：','Connected account is fully enabled for charges and payouts.'=>'已完全启用连接账户的收费和付款。','Stripe Connect status requires attention.'=>'Stripe 连接状态需要注意。','charges_enabled: %1$s, payouts_enabled: %2$s, currently_due: %3$d, past_due: %4$d.'=>'charges_enabled: %1$s, payouts_enabled: %2$s, currently_due: %3$d, past_due: %4$d.','Open connected account in Stripe'=>'在 Stripe 打开连接账户','Stripe Connect status check failed.'=>'Stripe 连接状态检查失败。','[removed]'=>'[已移除]','There was a problem removing your %1$s from order #%2$d.'=>'在订单 #%2$d 中移除您的 %1$s 时出现问题。','<p class="privacy-policy-tutorial">This sample language includes the basics around what personal data your PublishPress Cart installation may be collecting, storing and sharing, as well as who may have access to that data. Depending on what settings are enabled and which additional plugins are used, the specific information shared by your site will vary. We recommend consulting with a lawyer when deciding what information to disclose on your privacy policy.</p>
<h2>What we collect and store</h2>
<p>We collect information about you during the checkout process as well as some basic activities such as the dates you make purchases, or cancel your subscriptions with us.</p>
<p>While you visit our site, we’ll track:</p>
<ul>
   <li>— Products you’ve viewed:  we’ll use this to, for example, send you reminders about products you’ve recently viewed</li>
   <li>— IP address: we’ll use this for purposes like tracking which products you\'ve purchased and what discounts you’re eligible for</li>
   <li>— Name, email and physical address: we’ll ask you to enter this so we can communicate with you about your order and deliver your order to you!</li>
</ul>
<p>When you purchase from us, we’ll ask you to provide information including your name, billing/shipping address, email address, phone number, credit card/payment details and optional account information like username and password. We’ll use this information for purposes, such as, to:</p>
<ul>
   <li>— Send you information about your account and order</li>
   <li>— Respond to your requests, including refunds and complaints</li>
   <li>— Process payments and prevent fraud</li>
   <li>— Set up your account for our store</li>
   <li>— Improve our store offerings</li>
   <li>— Send you marketing messages, if you choose to receive them</li>
</ul>
<p>If you create an account, we will store your name, address, email and phone number, which will be used to populate the checkout for future orders.</p>
<p>We generally store information about you for as long as we need the information for the purposes for which we collect and use it, and we are not legally required to continue to keep it. For example, we will store order information for XXX years for tax and accounting purposes. This includes your name, email address and billing/shipping address.</p>
<h2>Who on our team has access</h2>
<p>Members of our team have access to the information you provide us. For example, site Owner/Administrators can access:</p>
<ul>
   <li>— Order information like what was purchased, subscription information, payment dates and amounts, and</li>
   <li>— Customer information like your name, username / email address, and address information.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our team members have access to this information to help fulfill orders, process refunds and support you.</p>
<h2>What we share with others</h2>
<p><em>
  In this section you should list who you’re sharing data with, and for what purpose. This could include, but may not be limited to, analytics/reporting tools, marketing services (such as email services like MailChimp, ActiveCampaign or Kit), payment gateways, and third party embeds.
</em></p>
<p><em>
We share information with third parties who help us provide additional contact services to you; for example – [enter your third party platforms such as Analytics, Email Marketing, or any others and short description of their purpose. If you have a DPA from that service, this would be a good place to include that also.]
</em></p>
<h3>Payments</h3>
<p class="privacy-policy-tutorial">In this subsection you should list which third party payment processors you’re using to take payments on your store since these may handle customer data. We’ve included Stripe as an example, but you should remove this if you’re not using Stripe.</p>
<p>We accept payments through Stripe. When processing payments, some of your data will be passed to Stripe, including information required to process or support the payment, such as the purchase total and billing information.</p>
<p>Please see the <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">Stripe Privacy Policy</a> for more details.</p>'=>'<p class="privacy-policy-tutorial">此示例语言包括有关您的 PublishPress 购物车安装可能收集、存储和共享的个人数据的基本信息，以及谁可能访问这些数据。根据启用的设置和使用的其他插件，您的网站共享的具体信息会有所不同。我们建议在决定在隐私政策中披露哪些信息时咨询律师。</p>
<h2>我们收集和存储的内容</h2>
<p>在结账过程中，我们会收集有关您的信息，以及您进行购买或取消订阅等基本活动的日期。</p>
<p>在您访问我们的网站时，我们将跟踪：</p>
<ul>
   <li>— 您查看过的产品：我们将利用这些信息，例如，向您发送关于您最近查看过的产品的提醒</li>
   <li>— IP 地址：我们将利用这些信息进行跟踪，例如，跟踪您购买了哪些产品以及您有资格获得哪些折扣</li>
   <li>— 姓名、电子邮件和地址：我们将要求您输入这些信息，以便我们能够与您沟通您的订单并将订单送达给您！</li>
</ul>
<p>当您向我们购买时，我们将要求您提供包括您的姓名、账单/送货地址、电子邮件地址、电话号码、信用卡/付款信息和可选帐户信息（如用户名和密码）在内的信息。我们将利用这些信息进行如下用途：</p>
<ul>
   <li>— 向您发送有关您的帐户和订单的信息</li>
   <li>— 回复您的请求，包括退款和投诉</li>
   <li>— 处理付款并防止欺诈</li>
   <li>— 为我们的商店设置您的帐户</li>
   <li>— 改进我们的商店产品</li>
   <li>— 向您发送营销信息，如果您选择接收这些信息</li>
</ul>
<p>如果您创建一个帐户，我们将存储您的姓名、地址、电子邮件和电话号码，这将用于填充未来订单的结账信息。</p>
<p>我们通常会存储关于您的信息，直到我们不再需要这些信息用于我们收集和使用它的目的，并且我们在法律上没有继续保留它的要求。例如，我们将存储订单信息 XXX 年以用于税务和会计目的。这包括您的姓名、电子邮件地址和账单/送货地址。</p>
<h2>我们团队中谁可以访问</h2>
<p>我们的团队成员可以访问您提供给我们的信息。例如，网站所有者/管理员可以访问：</p>
<ul>
   <li>— 订单信息，例如购买的商品、订阅信息、付款日期和金额，以及</li>
   <li>— 客户信息，例如您的姓名、用户名/电子邮件地址和地址信息。</li>
</ul>
<p>我们的团队成员可以访问这些信息，以帮助完成订单、处理退款和支持您。</p>
<h2>我们与他人分享的内容</h2>
<p><em>
  在此部分中，您应该列出您与谁共享数据，以及共享的目的。可能包括但不限于，分析/报告工具、营销服务（如电子邮件服务，如 MailChimp、ActiveCampaign 或 Kit）、支付网关和第三方嵌入。
</em></p>
<p><em>
我们与第三方共享信息，以帮助我们为您提供额外的联系服务；例如 - [输入您的第三方平台，例如分析、电子邮件营销或其他任何平台，以及它们目的的简短描述。如果您有该服务的 DPA，这也是一个很好的地方来包含它。]
</em></p>
<h3>支付</h3>
<p class="privacy-policy-tutorial">在此小节中，您应该列出您正在使用的第三方支付处理器，以便在您的商店中接受付款，因为这些可能会处理客户数据。我们已将 Stripe 作为示例，但如果您不使用 Stripe，请删除此内容。</p>
